{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"lineny-barathea-ladybug","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Suspected defect\n`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_verdict_cache.py` currently writes every concurrent producer for the same ticket and criterion through `<criterion-hash>.tmp`, then calls `os.replace` onto `<criterion-hash>.json`. The module claims last-write-wins safety, but the shared temporary pathname creates a plausible race: one writer can replace or overwrite the other writer's temporary file, and the outer best-effort exception handler can hide a lost cache write. This is a collision potential identified by source inspection, not a reproduced user-visible failure. It MUST be experimentally verified before any production change.\n\n## Mandatory reproduction before remediation\n1. Drive two independent writers for the same ticket and criterion with distinct, internally identifiable payloads. Use barriers around temporary-file write and `os.replace` so the overlap is deterministic; include a cross-process case because separate verifier processes share the cache directory.\n2. Record each writer's return value, exceptions before best-effort suppression, final JSON validity/content, and leftover temporary files. Distinguish harmless last-write-wins from a missing replace, payload cross-talk, invalid JSON, or silently lost cache population.\n3. If all forced interleavings are safe under the supported filesystems, record the falsification and close this bug without changing the writer. If an unsafe interleaving exists, preserve it as the failing regression test before remediation.\n\n## Remediation constraints if reproduced\n- Give every writer a unique temporary file in the destination directory (run id, UUID, or a secure same-directory temporary-file primitive), then retain atomic `os.replace` onto the shared final cache key.\n- A crash or failed replace must not leave a partial final JSON document; bounded cleanup may remove only that writer's own temporary file.\n- Cache failure remains an accelerator miss and must never alter the completion verdict.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic two-writer experiment proves or falsifies the collision across both thread/task and cross-process execution.\n- [ ] The experiment captures suppressed exceptions, writer results, final payload identity/JSON validity, and orphaned temporary files for each forced interleaving.\n- [ ] If reproduced, a regression test fails against the shared `<criterion-hash>.tmp` implementation before the fix.\n- [ ] If reproduced, writers use unique same-directory temporary paths and atomically replace the common final cache key without cross-writer cleanup.\n- [ ] Concurrent stress leaves one complete valid final record, no partial record, and no effect on the verifier verdict.\n- [ ] If the experiment falsifies the hypothesis, no production behavior is changed and the ticket closes with the falsifying evidence.","id":"7dea-2f00-db57-4a96","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["completion-verifier","concurrency","cache","experiment-first"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Parallel completion-cache writers may collide on a shared criterion .tmp path"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787678992088888001,"uuid":"3f3a1faa-eb01-487d-aa57-69fb2a0ab8ae"}